{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured the CentOS Stream 10 AppStream Redis-compatible Valkey service with durable AOF storage and a dedicated authenticated `inventory` identity. The generated credential remains undisclosed in `/etc/redis-inventory.env` with root-only permissions. A full node restart proved automatic service recovery and data persistence.","actions_performed":["Installed and enabled Valkey 8.1.7, CentOS Stream 10's supported Redis-compatible package.","Enabled AOF persistence with one-second fsync under `/var/lib/valkey`.","Generated a 256-bit credential on node1 and stored it in `/etc/redis-inventory.env` as `0600 root:root`.","Created the `inventory` ACL identity using only the credential hash in the service ACL file; disabled unauthenticated default access.","Applied persistent `vm.overcommit_memory=1` tuning.","Restarted node1 safely and verified its boot identity changed, the service recovered, and pre-restart data survived."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent Redis-compatible service","command_ids":["cmd-8b1e9faaccc84543","cmd-f7f3190d416442ca","cmd-86d3d2a2a5794e9d"],"summary":"Valkey is enabled and active; AOF with every-second fsync uses `/var/lib/valkey`. Startup logs show AOF replay, and the final persisted value is readable."},{"requirement":"Dedicated inventory identity and root-only generated credential","command_ids":["cmd-a37cdea3d885486a","cmd-26cbbc1c2c57427a","cmd-86d3d2a2a5794e9d"],"summary":"The generated 64-character hexadecimal credential is stored as `0600 root:root`; the ACL stores only its SHA-256 hash. Authenticated inventory access returns PONG while unauthenticated access returns NOAUTH."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-cb668907c92b459e","cmd-78dfcea460f440c8","cmd-2b3d1c7f6e474e2a","cmd-42732fed92c941a9","cmd-f7f3190d416442ca"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID was `d4784d1b-162e-4faa-b581-f6427617d23c`; reboot was acknowledged; post-restart boot ID became `7da2e6e2-1ac7-49bf-9a9f-823b75422cde`. Service, listener, authentication, AOF recovery, credential permissions, and stored data all recovered."}]}
